1
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:11,533
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:32,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,033
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,000
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,300
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:44,900
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:48,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,533
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,467
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,033 --> 00:00:55,600
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,567
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,367
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:02,633
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:09,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,200
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:12,900
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:15,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:21,567
<i>Domingo, transfer the gold
from your precinct</i>

21
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,100
<i> to the NLEA safe house.</i>

22
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:24,467
<i> Secure the gold bars.</i>

23
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,400
<i>It will be transferred
to the safe house tonight.</i>

24
00:01:26,533 --> 00:01:27,533
<i> Prepare a convoy.</i>

25
00:01:27,667 --> 00:01:28,667
<i> Happy birthday, Pa!</i>

26
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,600
<i>- Bottoms up!
- Hey!</i>

27
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:31,933
<i> What is going on here?!</i>

28
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:36,100
<i>And no one even bothered
to wake me up!</i>

29
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:37,733
<i> The party pooper has arrived.</i>

30
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:40,467
<i>Just because I wasn't able to
contribute to this celebration,</i>

31
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,867
<i> I'm the party pooper?</i>

32
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:43,400
<i> Django's here!</i>

33
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:45,600
<i>- Who's Django?
- He's my mortal enemy.</i>

34
00:01:45,733 --> 00:01:47,400
<i>I'm here
to offer you something.</i>

35
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:49,333
<i>- Sit down.
- We're here to invite you.</i>

36
00:01:49,467 --> 00:01:51,533
<i>A great deal of money
is at stake here.</i>

37
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:53,433
<i>- We're talking about gold.
- I'm a changed man now.</i>

38
00:01:53,567 --> 00:01:55,500
<i>And I don't really trust
your group.</i>

39
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,967
<i>You're refusing this offer?
Are you out of your mind?</i>

40
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,967
<i>It looks like we wasted
our time coming here.</i>

41
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,667
<i>This is my first time
seeing her around here.</i>

42
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,933
<i> - That's his wife.
</i>- You don't look good together.

43
00:02:06,433 --> 00:02:08,300
You people are unbelievable!

44
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:12,300
Money's being handed to you...

45
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:15,667
A blessing's being
handed to you,

46
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:18,000
and you still turn it down!

47
00:02:18,133 --> 00:02:19,833
You're so damn arrogant.

48
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:21,133
Hey, Betchay!

49
00:02:21,967 --> 00:02:24,767
If you worship money that much,

50
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,333
don't drag us into it.

51
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:31,333
Here's your gift.

52
00:02:31,467 --> 00:02:32,567
This?

53
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:34,033
[WRISTWATCH CLANKS]

54
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:35,067
You can have it back.

55
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,533
[MAMENG SCOFFS]

56
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:39,167
Fine, then! Don't take it!

57
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:40,867
You're given a gift,

58
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,667
and you still act all high
and mighty!

59
00:02:43,633 --> 00:02:44,533
What?!

60
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:46,867
Are you people so
innocent around here?

61
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,967
Have you never done
anything wrong?

62
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:51,333
Who do you think you are?

63
00:02:51,467 --> 00:02:53,967
You think you're all
some kind of angels?

64
00:02:54,767 --> 00:02:59,300
I'm the only devil
in this family, huh?

65
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:01,400
What?!
What are you all staring at?!

66
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:02,867
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- What?!

67
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,067
[MAMENG] Good grief!

68
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,400
That damn woman!

69
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:07,067
- [BETCHAY] Shut up!
- Oh, for god's sake!

70
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,267
Let her throw her tantrum!

71
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,133
She's so damn annoying!

72
00:03:11,267 --> 00:03:13,433
Does that woman have no shame?

73
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,667
Can you believe
she ruined your birthday?!

74
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,867
Well, she wants to show everyone

75
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,033
that she's better
than all of us here!

76
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:21,800
What I don't understand is...

77
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:24,000
Why did she get so pissed

78
00:03:24,133 --> 00:03:26,633
when Gabo turned down
Django's offer?

79
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:29,067
Of course it's because
of the money.

80
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,700
It's like you don't know
Betchay!

81
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:31,933
When it comes to money,

82
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,300
she doesn't care
what's right or wrong.

83
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:37,567
She really needs someone
who'll stand up to her

84
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:40,033
and give her a taste
of her own medicine!

85
00:03:41,133 --> 00:03:42,467
You know, Gabo...

86
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:43,767
Betchay won't leave you alone.

87
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:45,233
Believe me.

88
00:03:45,367 --> 00:03:48,433
Uncle, no matter what
Auntie Betchay says,

89
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:52,433
I'm not accepting the job
Django offered me.

90
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:56,867
Just ignore whatever
she says to you.

91
00:03:57,033 --> 00:04:00,400
Then she'll just target
Gloria instead.

92
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:01,900
[RUDY] Let her try!

93
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:04,067
She better not drag people

94
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,200
who have nothing
to do with this!

95
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,933
[GABO] Pa...

96
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,667
I don't care if Auntie Betchay
takes it out on me.

97
00:04:12,267 --> 00:04:14,267
She just better leave
Gloria out of it.

98
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,567
[MAMENG] Oh, dear.

99
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,000
You know what? We should
probably get some rest.

100
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:21,133
She might catch us here later.

101
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:22,300
Especially you, dear.

102
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:23,467
You should go inside now.

103
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,600
It's better not to give her
a reason to target you.

104
00:04:25,733 --> 00:04:26,767
Go on, dear.

105
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,567
- Go.
- Okay.

106
00:04:29,433 --> 00:04:32,400
Papa, happy birthday.

107
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:38,400
Love, I think you should
go ahead.

108
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:40,533
I'll follow you later.

109
00:04:40,667 --> 00:04:42,500
Papa and I have something
to talk about.

110
00:04:44,233 --> 00:04:46,600
- Let's go.
- Come on.

111
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:49,033
We'll go ahead.

112
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:50,600
[DJANGO] Move!

113
00:04:50,733 --> 00:04:52,367
That damn bastard Gabo!

114
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,400
How dare he turn down my offer!

115
00:04:55,533 --> 00:04:57,200
He's just like his father!

116
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:59,067
That Rudy should be grateful

117
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:01,433
I held myself back
because of Betchay!

118
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:05,800
Even though it's his birthday,
I would've shown him his place!

119
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:09,033
You know what?
We should all just relax.

120
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:10,667
Let's have a drink first.

121
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,633
It'll cool you down.

122
00:05:12,767 --> 00:05:19,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:27,433
Gabo, I'm glad
you refused Django's offer.

124
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:32,267
Papa, I'm not planning
to ruin my life again.

125
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:36,400
I know.

126
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,333
But I'm sure...

127
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:42,667
You also know
what turning him down means.

128
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,100
He's pissed.

129
00:05:44,867 --> 00:05:46,733
And there's something else
I noticed.

130
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:49,267
The way he was looking
at Gloria...

131
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,400
I noticed that too, Pa.

132
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,000
And I know what Django's like.

133
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,533
I won't let him get
anywhere near Gloria.

134
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,400
Son, be careful.

135
00:06:03,433 --> 00:06:05,467
You know they'll do
whatever it takes

136
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,267
to get what they want, okay?

137
00:06:11,433 --> 00:06:13,333
Too bad Gabo turned it down.

138
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:16,400
That's okay.

139
00:06:17,767 --> 00:06:20,500
Something good did come out
of us going there.

140
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:25,467
Pa, I understand you now.

141
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,467
About what?

142
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,633
That even though
Betchay's married,

143
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:35,300
you'll do anything
to steal her away.

144
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:39,200
That's exactly how I feel
about Gloria.

145
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:40,700
[PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

146
00:06:41,433 --> 00:06:44,533
Django,
you've finally found love.

147
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:47,600
But don't worry about that
for now.

148
00:06:48,267 --> 00:06:52,300
Focus on how we're going
to make money.

149
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:55,833
Pa, I won't mess up what
Mariano's asked us to do.

150
00:06:56,667 --> 00:06:57,800
But you know what?

151
00:06:58,567 --> 00:07:00,800
Gabo's only three steps
ahead of me.

152
00:07:00,933 --> 00:07:04,000
Once I'm rich,
I'll be way ahead of him.

153
00:07:04,533 --> 00:07:07,400
And I'll make sure
I steal Gloria away from him.

154
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:09,967
[LAUGHING MENACINGLY]

155
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,700
Then let the race begin.

156
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:18,667
But I think I'll catch Betchay
before you catch your Gloria.

157
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:20,767
[LAUGHING MENACINGLY]

158
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:22,033
[GLASSES CLINK]

159
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:27,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:07:27,267 --> 00:07:29,300
[BETCHAY]
You bunch of freeloaders!

161
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,767
What?

162
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,033
What the hell are you two
staring at?!

163
00:07:34,167 --> 00:07:37,733
I'm the one who ruined
the celebration again, huh?

164
00:07:37,867 --> 00:07:39,567
You're always the good ones!

165
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:42,000
You're always the ones
who never do anything wrong!

166
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:43,933
I'm always the bad one!

167
00:07:44,067 --> 00:07:45,800
- Who do you think you are?!
- Pa!

168
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:47,833
I've had enough! Let me go!

169
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:51,800
Betchay!

170
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:53,467
What's your problem?

171
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,900
You're my problem!

172
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,333
You and your son!

173
00:07:58,033 --> 00:08:02,300
The opportunity's right there,
being handed to you,

174
00:08:02,433 --> 00:08:03,967
and you still turned it down.

175
00:08:04,033 --> 00:08:05,700
Don't you understand?!

176
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:08,467
What they offered
was dangerous!

177
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,933
And I won't let Gabo
go to prison again

178
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:13,133
just to make money like that!

179
00:08:13,267 --> 00:08:16,167
[BETCHAY] All you ever say
is dangerous, dangerous!

180
00:08:16,967 --> 00:08:18,500
What's wrong with you?!

181
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:21,700
It's right there
in front of you!

182
00:08:21,867 --> 00:08:22,933
Money in your hands,

183
00:08:23,067 --> 00:08:25,100
and you still turn it
into nothing!

184
00:08:25,767 --> 00:08:27,400
What are you talking about?!

185
00:08:27,533 --> 00:08:28,733
Why?

186
00:08:28,867 --> 00:08:31,067
I do everything...

187
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:34,267
I do everything to provide
for this family.

188
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:39,200
Now you're being given a chance
to do your part!

189
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:42,167
To help the family!

190
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:44,533
And what did you do?

191
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:47,033
You turned it down!

192
00:08:47,167 --> 00:08:48,333
Why?

193
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:51,600
Because all you ever
think about is yourselves!

194
00:08:51,733 --> 00:08:53,333
It's always about you!

195
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:55,467
You don't care about
anyone else!

196
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:58,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:08:58,633 --> 00:08:59,733
Go on.

198
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:01,433
Go on!

199
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,433
Hurt me!

200
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:07,100
You can't do it.

201
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:16,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

202
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:27,800
[SAM]<i> I feel so sorry
</i> for Papa Rudy and Gabo.

203
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:33,767
<i>Auntie Betchay
treats them terribly.</i>

204
00:09:36,233 --> 00:09:38,467
<i>She humiliates them
in front of everyone.</i>

205
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,033
<i>She even ruins
their special occasions.</i>

206
00:09:40,167 --> 00:09:44,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,267
Let me go!

208
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,367
Hey!

209
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,767
The truth is finally out!

210
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,367
If you're going to replace me,

211
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,267
you could've at least gone for
someone prettier and younger!

212
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,867
How dare you, Paquito!

213
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,567
You're shameless!

214
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:03,400
What the hell is your problem?

215
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:05,200
You're not my wife!

216
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:07,100
How dare you, Paquito!

217
00:10:07,233 --> 00:10:09,400
How could you say that to me?!

218
00:10:09,533 --> 00:10:11,300
I do everything a wife does

219
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:13,000
and this is how you repay me?

220
00:10:13,133 --> 00:10:14,600
What's your problem?

221
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:17,300
I don't neglect you.

222
00:10:17,433 --> 00:10:19,300
I take good care of you!

223
00:10:19,433 --> 00:10:22,200
And that gives you the right
to cheat on me?!

224
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:23,500
Unbelievable.

225
00:10:23,633 --> 00:10:26,400
Are you trying to
humiliate me?!

226
00:10:26,533 --> 00:10:29,833
How could you humiliate me
like this?!

227
00:10:29,967 --> 00:10:31,733
That's why
I was hiding it from you.

228
00:10:31,867 --> 00:10:35,600
But you kept snooping around!

229
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:37,233
So it's my fault now?

230
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:39,233
Is this my fault, Paquito?!

231
00:10:39,367 --> 00:10:43,767
I dare you to bring
Betchay here.

232
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:46,333
I'll claw her face off.

233
00:10:46,467 --> 00:10:48,533
I'll paint the walls
with her blood!

234
00:10:48,667 --> 00:10:52,133
Mark my words, Paquito!

235
00:10:52,267 --> 00:10:53,533
Alright.

236
00:10:53,667 --> 00:10:56,433
I guess I can bring
Betchay here, then.

237
00:11:00,467 --> 00:11:02,533
- [PAQUITO GRUNTS]
- Don't you dare!

238
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,433
Don't you dare, Paquito!

239
00:11:04,567 --> 00:11:05,733
Ibyang!

240
00:11:06,567 --> 00:11:09,433
If you can't stand it,

241
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:10,767
leave!

242
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,800
[IBYANG WHIMPERS]

243
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:23,267
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,500
Ibyang.

245
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,267
You should go.

246
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,467
Go!

247
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,067
Come on!

248
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,767
[BOTTLES CLINK]

249
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,067
[IBYANG GRUNTS ANGRILY]

250
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,600
Santos, load these up.

251
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:47,700
- Yes, sir.
- You two.

252
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:48,933
- Sir?
- Suit up.

253
00:11:49,067 --> 00:11:50,700
- Yes, sir.
- Bring these down.

254
00:11:50,833 --> 00:11:54,000
Sir, we're getting ready
to transport the gold.

255
00:12:00,933 --> 00:12:03,100
Sir, is there a problem?

256
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:11,300
I can't believe General Jacinto
didn't trust us with the gold.

257
00:12:11,433 --> 00:12:14,400
He thinks we're going
to steal them.

258
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:18,733
Sir, bear with him.

259
00:12:18,867 --> 00:12:20,833
He's going through something.

260
00:12:20,967 --> 00:12:23,033
His daughter is still missing.

261
00:12:25,467 --> 00:12:26,933
Here's what we can do, sir.

262
00:12:27,067 --> 00:12:28,533
Let's do a good job.

263
00:12:28,667 --> 00:12:33,633
Let's deliver the gold to him
in perfect condition.

264
00:12:33,767 --> 00:12:35,333
Alright, sir?

265
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:39,433
I don't want to lose
General Jacinto's trust.

266
00:12:39,567 --> 00:12:41,033
Let's prove him wrong.

267
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:43,333
Copy that, sir.

268
00:12:43,467 --> 00:12:45,333
Sir, we'll finish loading
the shipment.

269
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:46,933
- Alright.
- Sir.

270
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:54,133
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:04,367
[GLASSES CLINK]

272
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,267
Oh, Tuko's here.

273
00:13:07,133 --> 00:13:09,867
So, were you able
to deploy more men?

274
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,067
Yes, boss.

275
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,467
We have men
monitoring NLEA for us.

276
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,567
Good.

277
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:19,967
Django, this is your chance

278
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,067
to prove to Boss Mariano

279
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:25,200
that you are my son!

280
00:13:26,067 --> 00:13:27,400
Of course, Pa!

281
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:30,933
I won't just prove
that you're my father,

282
00:13:31,067 --> 00:13:33,100
I will also exceed
their expectations.

283
00:13:33,233 --> 00:13:35,200
[BOTH LAUGH]

284
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:36,700
[GLASS THUDS]

285
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:37,900
Come on.

286
00:13:42,233 --> 00:13:43,800
Hey! Get back to work!

287
00:13:44,933 --> 00:13:48,767
[BETCHAY]
Don't you see it, Rudy?!

288
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:52,200
Gabo, are you sure
they're okay?

289
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:54,800
- It's getting heated out there.
- [RUDY] Really, Betchay?

290
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:56,333
Do you really think
that low of me?

291
00:13:56,467 --> 00:13:59,233
In case you've forgotten,
before I was shot,

292
00:13:59,367 --> 00:14:01,433
I was the one
who supported this family!

293
00:14:01,567 --> 00:14:02,633
Gabo and I!

294
00:14:02,767 --> 00:14:06,833
[BETCHAY] Oh, you barely
provided enough money.

295
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:09,967
We could barely make ends meet!

296
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,067
Why do you keep
holding it over me?!

297
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:16,333
Ever since you became
the manager at BeerGin,

298
00:14:16,867 --> 00:14:19,133
you've been blinded by money!

299
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:22,500
[BETCHAY] I've become
blinded by money?

300
00:14:23,033 --> 00:14:26,133
Where does the money I make
from BeerGin go?

301
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:28,100
To this family!

302
00:14:28,833 --> 00:14:34,600
Then your son brought home
another mouth to feed!

303
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:41,000
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:43,200
I don't know what to do
anymore, Gloria.

305
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,767
My poor father...

306
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:55,467
He doesn't deserve the way
Auntie Betchay treats him.

307
00:14:57,967 --> 00:15:00,433
She's already stepping
on his dignity.

308
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:05,133
It's like he's completely
useless to her.

309
00:15:06,133 --> 00:15:12,133
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

310
00:15:13,367 --> 00:15:18,300
Gabo, has Auntie Betchay
always been this way?

311
00:15:19,033 --> 00:15:21,000
Does she always
humiliate Papa Rudy

312
00:15:21,133 --> 00:15:22,700
in front of a lot of people?

313
00:15:23,533 --> 00:15:26,467
I don't know why
she's doing this to Papa.

314
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:30,367
It's like she wants
everyone to know

315
00:15:31,933 --> 00:15:34,500
that he's a worthless father

316
00:15:36,533 --> 00:15:38,533
because she's the one
who provides for our family.

317
00:15:38,667 --> 00:15:43,200
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:15:43,333 --> 00:15:45,300
But it's still wrong, Gabo.

319
00:15:46,267 --> 00:15:49,033
Even if she's the breadwinner,

320
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:52,367
she shouldn't treat
Papa Rudy that way.

321
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:56,900
I feel so bad for him.

322
00:15:58,033 --> 00:16:00,633
I can't blame Papa

323
00:16:03,133 --> 00:16:05,333
if he's finally had enough.

324
00:16:06,467 --> 00:16:09,300
He would never hurt
Auntie Betchay.

325
00:16:09,733 --> 00:16:11,800
But she's taken it too far.

326
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,867
She's being cruel.

327
00:16:18,367 --> 00:16:20,433
[BETCHAY]
I can't do this anymore!

328
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:24,867
I can't live like this anymore!

329
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,567
- I'm sick of you people!
- [VASE SHATTERS]

330
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,267
[SHOUTS ANGRILY]

331
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,267
[DOOR SLAMS]

332
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:33,867
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

333
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,367
Don't worry.

334
00:16:36,467 --> 00:16:41,867
One day, she'll realize that
what she's doing is wrong.

335
00:16:42,033 --> 00:16:43,600
She'll come to her senses.

336
00:16:44,367 --> 00:16:46,300
I'm really sorry.

337
00:16:46,433 --> 00:16:49,200
We don't know what to do
with Auntie Betchay anymore.

338
00:16:50,633 --> 00:16:53,000
We've been so understanding,

339
00:16:54,967 --> 00:16:56,833
but she won't change.

340
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,533
We just keep
putting up with her.

341
00:17:04,833 --> 00:17:08,000
We just take in
the harsh words she says.

342
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,700
I guess I'm to blame here.

343
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:16,433
She started treating us this way

344
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:20,933
ever since she lost her baby.

345
00:17:21,067 --> 00:17:27,933
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

346
00:17:28,733 --> 00:17:30,233
I'm sorry, Gloria.

347
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,400
[GLORIA SIGHS]

348
00:17:33,533 --> 00:17:35,300
Everything will be okay.

349
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,233
- Let's drink again.
- I'm not happy!

350
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:50,000
What a waste,
I was still admiring someone.

351
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,233
Who? The one who looks like ET?

352
00:17:51,233 --> 00:17:52,867
No, I don't like that.

353
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,867
- I'd rather punch that person.
- My dress is pretty, right?

354
00:17:54,867 --> 00:17:56,300
Yes. Where'd you buy it?

355
00:17:56,300 --> 00:18:03,200
[CHATTERING EXCITEDLY]

356
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:05,833
[KULOT] Pa! I got a lot!

357
00:18:05,833 --> 00:18:07,700
[BABOT]
Wow, my daughter got a lot!

358
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:10,100
We're rich today! We're rich!

359
00:18:11,467 --> 00:18:12,600
You're so great!

360
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:19,567
[PEOPLE SHOUTING]

361
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:23,733
All of you, listen up!

362
00:18:23,733 --> 00:18:26,033
If you don't bring out
who we're looking for,

363
00:18:26,033 --> 00:18:27,933
things will get messy for you!

364
00:18:27,933 --> 00:18:29,033
[MAN] Who are you, huh?!

365
00:18:29,767 --> 00:18:34,100
[BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

366
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:36,033
[MAN] Help us! Help! Help!

367
00:18:37,467 --> 00:18:38,500
Hey!

368
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:42,000
- What's going on?
- What's going on?!

369
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,033
What's going on?

370
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:47,233
Kulot! What happened?
Why are you crying?

371
00:18:47,233 --> 00:18:49,300
[KIDS CRYING]

372
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:51,367
[IPE]
Wait, we can't understand you.

373
00:18:51,367 --> 00:18:52,767
Kulot, talk to us.

374
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:57,900
They beat up Papa!
They even have guns!

375
00:18:57,933 --> 00:18:59,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [BABOT GRUNTS]

376
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:00,700
Where is she?

377
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,100
I don't know what you're saying!

378
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:03,667
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

379
00:19:03,667 --> 00:19:05,133
- [KIDS CRYING]
- Who?

380
00:19:05,133 --> 00:19:07,500
The ones who wanted to get
his organs? They went back?

381
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:12,300
I don't know.
But they're looking for someone.

382
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:14,367
Let's go! We have to tell Gabo!

383
00:19:14,367 --> 00:19:16,033
Let's hide you first.
You have to hide.

384
00:19:16,033 --> 00:19:17,233
Hide the kids, quick!

385
00:19:17,233 --> 00:19:20,233
We don't have to call Gabo.
We have guns, anyway!

386
00:19:20,233 --> 00:19:22,333
We have to call Gabo, Tekla.

387
00:19:23,367 --> 00:19:25,600
- Fine! We have to hurry!
- Let's go.

388
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,867
- Let's go! Run!
- Let's go!

389
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:28,433
Run!

390
00:19:29,767 --> 00:19:32,500
Will that take long? Hurry up!

391
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:35,700
Make sure the gold gets
to the safe house.

392
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:36,767
Yes, sir.

393
00:19:37,633 --> 00:19:38,767
Hurry, hurry!

394
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,700
[VAN DOORS SHUT]

395
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,233
- [POLICE] Sir, it's done.
- Roll out!

396
00:19:45,433 --> 00:19:48,767
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

397
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,033
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

398
00:19:52,033 --> 00:19:53,400
Sir.

399
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,567
Where will they bring
the Zafras' gold?

400
00:19:55,567 --> 00:19:57,600
Your father's orders
are to bring the gold,

401
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:59,800
and secure it
in the safe house.

402
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,800
Sir, permission to join
the convoy.

403
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,233
Sir, this is
a high-risk operation!

404
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,067
They'll need more men!

405
00:20:06,067 --> 00:20:08,667
Officer Umali and his men
can handle it.

406
00:20:08,667 --> 00:20:12,067
Sir, this is personal and
very important for my father.

407
00:20:12,067 --> 00:20:14,767
The Zafras are the suspects
in my sister's ambush.

408
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:17,233
Please, let me be part
of this case.

409
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:19,500
Okay. Okay!

410
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,767
You can follow them
if you like,

411
00:20:20,767 --> 00:20:22,067
but bring your team.

412
00:20:22,067 --> 00:20:23,733
- Thank you, sir. Yes, sir.
- Alright?

413
00:20:23,733 --> 00:20:24,833
Estrella, let's go.

414
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:26,833
[SIGHS]

415
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:28,333
[PHONE RINGING]

416
00:20:29,267 --> 00:20:30,933
- Hello?
- [MAN] Boss.

417
00:20:30,933 --> 00:20:32,367
They just left.

418
00:20:32,367 --> 00:20:33,733
Okay, we'll get ready.

419
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:36,267
They're coming!

420
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:37,900
Get to your positions, quick!

421
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:43,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

422
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:44,767
Get to your positions!

423
00:20:44,767 --> 00:20:47,633
[GATE CREAKING, THUDS]

424
00:20:48,933 --> 00:20:55,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

425
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:59,833
[ESTRELLA] Are you sure
we should go with the convoy?

426
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:02,233
I'm not forcing you
if you don't want to go.

427
00:21:02,233 --> 00:21:03,700
Ma'am, I'm just worried
about you.

428
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:05,667
You already have a lot
on your plate.

429
00:21:05,667 --> 00:21:07,100
You are still looking
for your sister,

430
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:09,200
you're handling her case,
and now--

431
00:21:09,233 --> 00:21:12,100
Estrella, I'm not just
doing this for Sam.

432
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,267
It's also for Dad.

433
00:21:13,267 --> 00:21:14,667
He wants
to hold the Zafras accountable

434
00:21:14,667 --> 00:21:15,933
for what happened to my sister,

435
00:21:15,933 --> 00:21:17,933
and this is one of the ways
I can hold them accountable.

436
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:20,567
If I have to be the one
to finish this for my family...

437
00:21:21,933 --> 00:21:23,267
I'd do it.

438
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:25,267
- Men, let's go!
- Move!

439
00:21:25,267 --> 00:21:27,833
- [CAR DOORS OPENING]
- [ENGINES STARTING]

440
00:21:27,833 --> 00:21:30,767
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

441
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:32,433
[IPE] Gabo! Gabo!

442
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,000
- Move!
- Gabo!

443
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,233
- Gabo! Move! Gabo!
- Gabo!

444
00:21:37,233 --> 00:21:41,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

445
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:42,567
Why?

446
00:21:43,533 --> 00:21:44,600
[SAM] Gabo!

447
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:48,233
[TOLITS] Gabo! Gabo!

448
00:21:48,233 --> 00:21:50,600
- Gabo, we need your help.
- Why?

449
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,367
Someone broke into
Mister Babot's home.

450
00:21:52,367 --> 00:21:54,767
The ones who took them before
might be back!

451
00:21:55,367 --> 00:21:56,433
Wait!

452
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:01,800
- Gloria, stay here.
- Where are you going?

453
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:03,800
Gabo!

454
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:05,467
- Gabo!
- [GABO] Come on!

455
00:22:05,467 --> 00:22:06,967
- Let's go.
- They're dead to us.

456
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,467
What's happening, Gabo?
Why are you mad again?

457
00:22:10,467 --> 00:22:11,633
What's happening?

458
00:22:11,633 --> 00:22:13,867
Gabo suddenly left
when his friends called for him!

459
00:22:13,867 --> 00:22:15,833
- Where is he going?
- I don't know.

460
00:22:15,867 --> 00:22:18,500
What's going on?
Why's there too much noise?

461
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:20,633
- Gabo just suddenly left.
- Huh?!

462
00:22:20,633 --> 00:22:22,333
[DANTE] He might go to Django.

463
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:25,367
Why would he go to Django?
They're not fighting!

464
00:22:25,367 --> 00:22:27,167
[RUDY] Dante, come with me.
Let's follow Gabo.

465
00:22:27,167 --> 00:22:28,800
Hey, hey, hey, hey,
Rudy, don't.

466
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,500
Don't leave.
It might get worse!

467
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:34,000
Let's just wait for Gabo
to come back.

468
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

469
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:39,900
- [MAN] Help!
- Move! Move!

470
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,567
- Where are they?!
- There, Gabo!

471
00:22:41,567 --> 00:22:42,933
[WOMAN] Help us!

472
00:22:45,967 --> 00:22:46,933
[BLOW LANDS]

473
00:22:46,933 --> 00:22:51,467
[PEOPLE SHOUTING, CRYING]

474
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,433
Save the kids.
I'll save Mister Babot!

475
00:22:53,433 --> 00:22:55,100
- [WOMAN] Help!
- Let's go!

476
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:56,467
- Come on, let's go!
- Save the kids!

477
00:22:57,300 --> 00:23:04,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

478
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:06,667
You've got a lot of nerve...

479
00:23:07,767 --> 00:23:09,833
to step foot
in Ginintuang Lupa.

480
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:18,867
- [SCREAMS]
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

481
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,600
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [KICK LANDS]

482
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:22,733
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

483
00:23:22,867 --> 00:23:24,233
Gabo's here!

484
00:23:24,367 --> 00:23:25,333
[MAN GRUNTING]

485
00:23:25,467 --> 00:23:26,800
[BLOW LANDS, KICK LANDS]

486
00:23:28,933 --> 00:23:30,200
[BLOWS LANDING]

487
00:23:31,533 --> 00:23:32,700
[KICK LANDS]

488
00:23:34,233 --> 00:23:35,233
[BODY THUDS]

489
00:23:36,067 --> 00:23:37,533
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [KICK LANDS]

490
00:23:37,667 --> 00:23:38,700
[KNIFE SWOOSH]

491
00:23:38,833 --> 00:23:39,933
[KICK LANDS]

492
00:23:43,833 --> 00:23:44,800
[KICK LANDS]

493
00:23:44,933 --> 00:23:46,800
Thank God he came!

494
00:23:46,933 --> 00:23:48,233
[KICK LANDS]

495
00:23:50,733 --> 00:23:51,733
[KICK LANDS]

496
00:23:52,267 --> 00:23:53,433
[KICK LANDS]

497
00:23:54,667 --> 00:23:55,800
[KNIFE SWOOSH]

498
00:23:55,967 --> 00:23:57,033
[KICK LANDS]

499
00:23:58,067 --> 00:23:59,133
[GLASS SHATTERS]

500
00:24:01,967 --> 00:24:03,033
[KICK LANDS]

501
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,333
[TABLE THUDS]

502
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:09,267
Pa, maybe we should go
and check on Gabo?

503
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,600
Oh, dear, we can't.

504
00:24:10,733 --> 00:24:13,267
You don't know the people
in here well enough.

505
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:15,867
We understand how you feel,

506
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,267
but we might make
the situation worse.

507
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,367
Don't go in there, dear.

508
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,800
She's right, Gloria.

509
00:24:21,933 --> 00:24:23,367
Don't worry about Gabo.

510
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:25,567
He got this. Gabo will be okay.

511
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:29,167
I'm just worried
that they ganged up on him.

512
00:24:29,333 --> 00:24:30,900
He's with friends.

513
00:24:31,033 --> 00:24:33,300
They'll look after him.

514
00:24:33,433 --> 00:24:35,000
They wouldn't dare.

515
00:24:35,133 --> 00:24:37,033
If something bad happens
to my son,

516
00:24:37,167 --> 00:24:38,400
they'd better go into hiding.

517
00:24:38,533 --> 00:24:43,900
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

518
00:24:44,033 --> 00:24:46,733
[MAMENG] Hey, hey, hey,
where are you going?

519
00:24:46,867 --> 00:24:48,500
I just need some fresh air.

520
00:24:49,433 --> 00:24:50,900
I'll wait for my husband.

521
00:24:53,733 --> 00:24:55,000
[RUDY] Okay.

522
00:24:57,533 --> 00:25:00,100
Rudy, did you hear that?

523
00:25:00,233 --> 00:25:02,333
She thinks
she's really married to him.

524
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,933
Of course. We told her that.

525
00:25:05,067 --> 00:25:06,933
Obviously, she believed it.

526
00:25:07,067 --> 00:25:09,267
What if they really fall in love
with each other?

527
00:25:10,200 --> 00:25:13,033
Dante, I'm more worried
about Gabo.

528
00:25:13,167 --> 00:25:15,733
He might really be
falling for Gloria.

529
00:25:15,867 --> 00:25:19,133
What if one day he just
wakes up in this dream?

530
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:21,167
That none of this is real.

531
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:23,333
And realize that
this is unlikely to happen.

532
00:25:24,367 --> 00:25:25,433
[RUDY SIGHS]

533
00:25:31,067 --> 00:25:32,733
[SAM] I'm worried about Gabo.

534
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:35,333
<i>What if something bad
happens to him?</i>

535
00:25:41,133 --> 00:25:43,867
Why am I so concerned about him?

536
00:25:46,333 --> 00:25:48,667
<i>I can't help
getting close to his family.</i>

537
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,700
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [YELLS]

538
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:54,367
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GROANS]

539
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:55,667
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

540
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,267
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GABO GROANS]

541
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:00,367
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

542
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,567
[BODY THUDS]

543
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:09,467
[BLOW LANDS]

544
00:26:13,533 --> 00:26:15,100
- [YELLS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

545
00:26:15,233 --> 00:26:16,633
[GABO GROANS]

546
00:26:16,767 --> 00:26:18,533
- Please stop!
- Stop!

547
00:26:19,367 --> 00:26:26,333
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

548
00:26:30,600 --> 00:26:32,433
<i> Boss Mariano called me.</i>

549
00:26:32,567 --> 00:26:34,833
<i>- He'll have you picked up.
- This is my chance.</i>

550
00:26:34,967 --> 00:26:37,033
<i>I'll go on with the plan
to make Gabo the fall guy.</i>

551
00:26:37,167 --> 00:26:38,833
<i>Where were you?
Were you on the job?</i>

552
00:26:38,967 --> 00:26:41,733
<i>Don't mess with us!
What do you need from us?!</i>

553
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,367
<i> I knew you were on it!</i>

554
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:46,167
<i> This is important to her.</i>

555
00:26:46,300 --> 00:26:49,600
<i>This is Sam's watch. It was
given to her by her brother RJ.</i>

556
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:50,500
<i>- Is this expensive?
- Huh?</i>

557
00:26:50,633 --> 00:26:51,700
<i> I mean, important?</i>

558
00:26:51,833 --> 00:26:56,167
<i>We're here again to settle
and offer compensation.</i>

559
00:26:56,300 --> 00:26:59,500
<i> I hope you sign this document</i>

560
00:26:59,633 --> 00:27:02,567
saying that this is all settled.

561
00:27:02,700 --> 00:27:03,500
<i> My father won't settle.</i>

562
00:27:03,633 --> 00:27:05,167
<i> And we won't take your money!</i>

563
00:27:05,300 --> 00:27:08,100
<i>If possible, please don't show
your faces here again!</i>

564
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:09,167
<i> Seems like anytime soon,</i>

565
00:27:09,300 --> 00:27:10,600
<i>the decision
will be in our favor.</i>

566
00:27:10,733 --> 00:27:12,800
<i>I can finally demolish
all of Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

567
00:27:14,933 --> 00:27:16,000
[GUN COCKS]

568
00:27:21,933 --> 00:27:23,200
[GUNSHOT]

569
00:27:23,333 --> 00:27:24,633
<i> I'm sorry, Ricardo.</i>

570
00:27:24,767 --> 00:27:26,700
<i>NCIA didn't look after
my daughter.</i>

571
00:27:26,833 --> 00:27:29,000
<i>You knew how dangerous
the Zafra case is!</i>

572
00:27:29,133 --> 00:27:31,600
Yet you still let her handle it!
<i> And now she's gone!</i>

573
00:27:32,433 --> 00:27:35,900
<i>I failed to make her feel
that she's my daughter.</i>

574
00:27:36,600 --> 00:27:38,267
<i> Now, I...</i>

575
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:41,667
I'm asking for a second chance.

576
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:43,400
<i> Just come back, Sam.</i>

577
00:27:43,533 --> 00:27:46,367
<i>I'll make you feel
how much I love you.</i>

578
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:49,567
<i>We caught them.
They're outsiders.</i>

579
00:27:49,733 --> 00:27:51,000
<i>- Beat them up!
- Come on!</i>

580
00:27:52,233 --> 00:27:54,700
<i>Hold on! Hold on!
Why are you here?</i>

581
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,333
<i> Pops asked us to come here.</i>

582
00:27:56,467 --> 00:27:59,800
<i>Tomorrow, we'll send you
the details of your mission.</i>

583
00:27:59,933 --> 00:28:00,867
<i> You can't fail.</i>

584
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,500
<i>Prove that you're worthy
of his trust.</i>

585
00:28:03,633 --> 00:28:05,800
<i>I'll do everything
to succeed in my mission.</i>

586
00:28:05,933 --> 00:28:06,933
<i> Gabo?</i>
